Z||000000||flipperwasaporpoise||05-31-2001||10:06 PM||||Should I trade my 85 V6 4sp for an 88 4-cyl automatic?  Keep in mind that I don't care if my car is fast.  The Fiero I have now is in good mechanical shape, white, but it's really boring looking.  The other one is black, in good mechanical shape as well, and has t-tops and just looks a lot better.  Of course, my car is faster and funner to drive.   Does this sound like a good deal??  I sort of have my mind made up, but I would like to know what others think.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Urchin||05-31-2001||10:10 PM||||If it were me I would dress up my existing car, if the time and money is there.  It's much more satisfying to dress your own up your own way (my opinion).  If your car is reliable, then I would put some money into cosmetics.  But if you can get a deal on the other one and don't have the money to fix up your own, then I'd buy it.  That's my thoughts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_8.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||flipperwasaporpoise||05-31-2001||10:16 PM||||I was thinking the same thing, about it being more satisfying to fix up your own car.  I don't know if I want to spend the money..I don't know.  Oh well, I guess I'll just see what happens.||||reg||1
