Z||000008||AusFiero||06-01-2001||09:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>If the ttops are in VERY GOOD shape ok if not pass- ttops parts are just about non-existent</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Tell me about it. It cost me $3000 AUS to replace my right hand t-top and to buy a new main rubbers kit. The rubbers are sitting in my bedroom awaiting use some day as mine only leak slightly and the car doesn't go out in the rain anyway. Didn't need them when I bought them but figured hey, they are one of the last new sets left, get em while ya can.<P>Mind you, still wouldn't give up my t-tops for anything.<P>If anyone is interested I know where there is a complete t-top kit out of a 1988 Fiero. It is for sale for about $800 US plus shipping. Shipping being the dear bit as it is in Australia. Expect $250 US shipping costs.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||1
