Z||000010||montage||06-01-2001||11:27 AM||||Another issue is the handling difference. When I was looking at Fiero's I drove a 85 GT and then decided on an 88 formula. The formula handles much better (especially no bump steer) than the 85 and this was before I fixed a broken end link on rear sway bar and two different and wrong end links on the front with M&S tires on the 88. The 88 coupe doesn't have the rear sway bar but that  can be put added. I go for the 88 if the t-tops are good.||||reg||1
